CONCEPT
  product        Quill, Model H
  one-liner      An autonomous ground-mobility stack for hedgehogs. Your hedgehog keeps walking.
                 The road becomes our problem.
  premise        The company has classified a live animal as a vehicle and never acknowledges it.
                 Full Self-Crossing (Supervised), where "supervised" means a human must stand at
                 the roadside for the whole crossing, which was the original problem.
  demo concept   In-vehicle console: top-down night driving visualisation of one hedgehog crossing
                 a residential B-road, perception layer classifying kerb, drain grate, parked
                 hatchback, badger, and a cat it can only call UNKNOWN OBJECT at 0.38.

DESIGN DIRECTION
  style          Photographic automotive press-configurator, night-shift dark mode
  archetype      Interactive configurator / EV manufacturer product page (ui-ux-pro-max returned
                 "Interactive 3D Configurator" for the query; pattern kept, its default light
                 slate + action-red palette and Rubik/Nunito pairing discarded as generic and as
                 a near-collision with 2026-08-28's arterial red)
  palette        primary #3BE08A charge green (sole carrier), accent #35C8E8 perception cyan
                 (quarantined to the perception layer), bg #12161A wet asphalt, fg/ink #E7ECEF,
                 muted #8A959D
  fonts          display Sora, body Manrope, figures Martian Mono
  motifs         perception bracket (four cyan corner ticks + mono label + confidence figure
                 wrapping every frame); charge bar (24 cells, used as range meter, list bullet,
                 pricing gauge, crossing progress)
  motion         one headlamp sweep across the hero on load, bracket snap on hover, charge cells
                 fill on scroll, 1px CTA depress, 6px section fade-up. All behind
                 prefers-reduced-motion.

