  verdict: no collision on style, palette, or font pairing. Sora, Manrope and Martian Mono are
  unused in the last 7. bg #12161A is a cold blue slate, clearly separated from the three recent
  dark grounds (#0D1712, #0B0C0B, #0F1220). Charge green as a carrier is unused recently; a
  warm red or amber accent was deliberately avoided because 08-31, 08-30, 08-29 and 08-28 all
  spent their rationed colour there.

IMAGES
  allocation     4 of 4 used. 1 hero (16:9) + 3 testimonial unit portraits (1:1). No demo assets.
  rationale      Hero earned it outright: a manufacturer page is carried by one enormous night
                 product shot, so the hedgehog is photographed like a press car on wet asphalt.
                 Demo assets skipped because the demo screen is a rendered driving visualisation
                 built in CSS, and a photograph inside it would fight the perception layer.
                 Remaining budget went to the testimonial plates. The owner quotes are human, so
                 the bracket-framed photograph is the vehicle under review rather than the
                 reviewer, captioned with the owner's name and unit number in mono.
  hero.webp      1 attempt. PASS. Hedgehog in profile on wet asphalt, hard raking key light,
                 cold falloff, green road-line reflection at the right edge. Correct press-car
                 framing, no text artifacts, palette harmonises.
  unit-1.webp    1 attempt. PASS. Head-on badge portrait, cyan edge light, deadpan.
  unit-2.webp    1 attempt. PASS. Three-quarter view. Framing is closer to full-body than
                 head-and-shoulders, which reads fine at 64px in the testimonial plate.
  unit-3.webp    1 attempt. PASS. Low angle, snout raised, cyan top light.
  no regenerations required. All four cropped to spec, all well under the 500 KB ceiling
  (hero 174 KB, units 20-27 KB).

