VISUAL CHECK (step 9, ran)
  playwright present. 2 captures of index.html, 3 corrective edits, all caps respected.
  finding    first capture showed the hero only. Every section below it was blank. The .rv
             scroll-reveal hides content at opacity 0 and only unhides it when the
             IntersectionObserver fires, so any path where it does not fire (full-page capture,
             scripting disabled, observer never triggered) rendered the page as a hero and a
             footer. Real breakage, not taste.
  fix        (1) scoped the hiding rules under .js so no-script readers get the content;
             (2) set that class from a one-line head script, so there is no flash of hidden
             content; (3) added a 1600ms net that reveals anything the observer has not.
  recapture  confirmed. Hero, spec strip, three feature plates with perception readouts,
             testimonials with bracket-framed unit portraits, three trim tiers with charge
             gauges, CTA band and footer all render. No overlap, no off-canvas element, no
             wrong aspect ratio, contrast holds.
  left alone pricing perk bullets read slightly wide, and the Sentry readout carries more
             vertical air than the other two. Taste, not breakage, so untouched.
  revalidated after the edits -> OK (exit 0)
